Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:36:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 017/106] Revert: remove the smart-amp AFE experiment from
 q6afe_dai_prepare()

Attempt 3 (sending the TI smart-amp CAPI enable param after
q6afe_port_start()) did not produce sound and was never shown to do
anything useful - it just logged ret=0. It is a prime suspect for
actively breaking playback: it tells the DSP to enable a vendor
smart-amp module on TERTIARY_MI2S_RX that mainline's AFE topology
does not actually contain, which could plausibly swallow the PCM
stream while every command still returns success.

Removing it so the port runs a plain, unmodified AFE config. The
q6afe_send_generic_param() helper stays in q6afe.c (unused) - the
send mechanism itself was verified working, only this call site was
speculative.
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c | 22 ----------------------
 1 file changed, 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
index 45c19d101..b6b09c267 100644
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6afe-dai.c
@@ -443,28 +443,6 @@ static int q6afe_dai_prepare(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 	}
 	dai_data->is_port_started[dai->id] = true;
 
-	/*
-	 * EXPERIMENTAL (attempt 3): register TI's TAS256x smart-amp AFE
-	 * module with the DSP, now that the port's own real config has
-	 * been sent and AFE_PORT_CMD_DEVICE_START has already succeeded -
-	 * two earlier attempts sending this during the machine driver's
-	 * .startup (before any of that) broke the pipeline (hw_params
-	 * started failing with -EINVAL), regardless of a port refcounting
-	 * fix, pointing at command ordering rather than a refcount bug.
-	 */
-	if (dai->id == TERTIARY_MI2S_RX) {
-		u32 smartamp_payload[14] = { 1, };
-		int sret;
-
-		sret = q6afe_send_generic_param(dai_data->port[dai->id],
-			0x11111112 /* AFE_SMARTAMP_MODULE_RX */,
-			0x10012D13 /* CAPI_V2_TAS_RX_ENABLE */,
-			smartamp_payload, sizeof(smartamp_payload));
-		dev_info(dai->dev,
-			"tas smartamp enable experiment (post-start): %d\n",
-			sret);
-	}
-
 	return 0;
 }
 
